listings.body:
Help me plan how to learn {{subject}}.

My goal: {{goal}}
Time available: {{time available:about 4 hours a week}}
What I already know: {{background:not much}}

Create a week-by-week plan that:
- breaks the subject into small milestones,
- mixes learning with practice and short reviews of earlier material,
- says how I can tell each milestone is done.

Keep it realistic for the time I have. Ask me one clarifying question first if something important is missing.

Draft an email to {{recipient}} about {{purpose}}.

Tone: {{tone:friendly and professional}}
Key points to include: {{key points}}

Keep it under 150 words, put the request in the first two sentences, and suggest a subject line. Give two alternative versions of the opening sentence.

I need to decide: {{decision}}

Options I am considering: {{options}}
What matters most to me: {{priorities}}

For each option, list the main benefits, costs and risks, and what would have to be true for it to be the best choice. Then ask me the three questions that would most help me decide. Do not make the decision for me.

I am getting this problem in {{language or framework}}:

What I expected: {{expected}}
What happens instead: {{actual}}
Error message (if any): {{error:none}}

Relevant code:
```
{{code}}
```

List the most likely causes in order, with a quick check for each that would confirm or rule it out. Then suggest a fix for the most likely cause. If you need more information, say exactly what.

Help me reply to this customer message for {{business name}}:

"""
{{customer message}}
"""

What we can offer: {{what we can offer}}

Write a reply that acknowledges their concern, explains clearly what we will do and by when, and stays within what we can offer — do not promise anything else. Keep it warm and under 150 words.
